01:02:37.340 --> 01:02:46.860
All they wanted to do was go to this special little sleeping nook that Daryl told them about in the warehouse, and now they're overhearing Dwight and Angela.

1218
01:02:46.860 --> 01:02:52.160
So I have to tell you, getting to our sleeping spot was actually very complicated.

1219
01:02:52.520 --> 01:02:54.160
Yeah, you guys are up really high.

1220
01:02:54.420 --> 01:02:54.840
Yes.

1221
01:02:54.860 --> 01:02:57.960
We are actually up on a shelf in the warehouse.

1222
01:02:57.960 --> 01:03:00.300
It's a special thing that they built.

1223
01:03:00.840 --> 01:03:08.280
Randy reminded me that we actually had to practice getting up there using a scissor lift.

1224
01:03:08.280 --> 01:03:09.000
Wow.

1225
01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:17.020
And it involved a whole rehearsal the week prior with a Universal Studios safety officer named Ian Bass Gillespie.

1226
01:03:17.540 --> 01:03:23.960
This person was in attendance to sign off on our use of the scissor lift, and it was a big deal.

1227
01:03:24.160 --> 01:03:32.480
But we made it up there, and we're laying truly up on this high shelf in this little nook.

1228
01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:36.500
And I will tell you right now, it was so comfy cozy.

1229
01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:40.540
It was everything that Daryl advertised it to be.

1230
01:03:40.840 --> 01:03:47.060
And it was a dream to just sort of get to kind of nap for part of my workday.

1231
01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:51.780
All I could think about when I saw you guys up there was, what if you have to pee?

1232
01:03:54.240 --> 01:03:55.760
That's what I always think.

1233
01:03:56.220 --> 01:03:57.680
Like, could you imagine?

1234
01:03:57.860 --> 01:04:01.120
That is why I never want to sleep on the top bunk of a bunk bed.

1235
01:04:01.120 --> 01:04:01.960
I know!

1236
01:04:02.400 --> 01:04:05.300
Well, we had a fan question from Michelle S.

1237
01:04:05.460 --> 01:04:09.320
in Melbourne, Australia that I thought was very wise.

1238
01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:10.900
Michelle said,

1239
01:04:11.180 --> 01:04:17.340
The spot where the warehouse guys take their naps is right above Dwight and Angela's sex spot.

1240
01:04:17.660 --> 01:04:21.940
Does this mean that the warehouse guys know about Dwight and Angela's affair?

1241
01:04:22.260 --> 01:04:22.640
Ah!

1242
01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:25.720
I mean, they've been there the whole time.

1243
01:04:25.960 --> 01:04:26.340
Ah!

1244
01:04:26.860 --> 01:04:29.480
I think the warehouse guys do know about your affair.

1245
01:04:29.740 --> 01:04:30.740
Oh, for sure.

1246
01:04:31.120 --> 01:04:34.980
I don't think you guys are hiding it from them at all.

1247
01:04:35.280 --> 01:04:38.420
Clearly, we haven't been hiding it very well from anyone.

1248
01:04:38.920 --> 01:04:39.460
Exactly.

1249
01:04:41.280 --> 01:04:46.620
Well, the episode is going to end with Michael exiting the building, and he's approached by a news team.

1250
01:04:46.960 --> 01:04:48.080
The reporter says,

1251
01:04:48.200 --> 01:04:50.680
Michael Scott, do you want to make a comment on the rumors?

1252
01:04:51.380 --> 01:04:52.420
Michael sighs.

1253
01:04:52.740 --> 01:04:53.200
He's like,

1254
01:04:53.200 --> 01:04:59.180
I have done some very bad things, things of which I am not proud.

1255
01:04:59.260 --> 01:05:09.040
I would like to publicly apologize to the coach and the players, and I vow to never listen to my bodily instincts ever again.

1256
01:05:09.040 --> 01:05:11.980
The reporter is confused.

1257
01:05:12.060 --> 01:05:12.620
The reporter is confused.

1258
01:05:12.620 --> 01:05:13.640
She says,

1259
01:05:14.300 --> 01:05:17.260
I'm talking about the saber printers that catch on fire.

1260
01:05:17.900 --> 01:05:18.840
And Michael's like,

1261
01:05:18.940 --> 01:05:20.400
Oh, okay, I was talking about,

1262
01:05:20.540 --> 01:05:21.200
Wait, wait, what?

1263
01:05:21.780 --> 01:05:22.340
Yeah.

1264
01:05:22.340 --> 01:05:28.080
So, Randy told me that this was like a standards and practices issue.

1265
01:05:28.340 --> 01:05:28.900
This scene.

1266
01:05:29.120 --> 01:05:29.660
Why?

1267
01:05:30.040 --> 01:05:31.460
That's what I asked.

1268
01:05:31.640 --> 01:05:36.700
He said that they wanted us to create a fictitious news channel.

1269
01:05:37.480 --> 01:05:41.940
They didn't want us to use the real NBC affiliate, which is WBRE.

1270
01:05:42.760 --> 01:05:46.780
But we had established WBRE in the show before.

1271
01:05:47.540 --> 01:05:53.860
So, they had to get a signed clearance agreement from the real WBRE in Scranton.

1272
01:05:54.560 --> 01:06:00.640
And eventually, we were given a pass so that we could use the actual call letters in the show.

1273
01:06:01.350 --> 01:06:01.780
Oh, yeah.

1274
01:06:01.900 --> 01:06:03.960
And you can see it very clearly on the microphone.

1275
01:06:04.220 --> 01:06:04.640
Mm-hmm.

1276
01:06:04.920 --> 01:06:05.360
Yeah.

1277
01:06:05.360 --> 01:06:10.340
Well, this is going to set up a huge story arc now for Michael.

1278
01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:15.340
He's going to end up being the spokesperson for Saber.

1279
01:06:15.900 --> 01:06:17.200
Joe is going to come back.

1280
01:06:17.400 --> 01:06:20.980
It's all going to go down next week in the whistleblower.

1281
01:06:21.880 --> 01:06:22.360
Yes.

1282
01:06:22.580 --> 01:06:25.780
The season finale whistleblower.

1283
01:06:26.600 --> 01:06:28.020
Well, that was the chump.

1284
